rts occupancy agrees with the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]admission gate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]monitor_runner_slots.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/monitor_runner_slots.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ps[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ps/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Occupancy rule and live admission gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]count[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]count: separate slot occupancy from slot admission in the pure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runner-slot core, make a serial agent family hold one slot while any of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its shells (agent or monitor) is live, and wire the live admission gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the new count.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Occupancy parity across ACE and agent listings[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]display[dim] · [dim][/dim]after count[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]display: make the ACE capacity chip, statistics methodology text, wait [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal, and agent listings report the same occupancy the admission gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforces, including rows for post-handoff family shells that are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invisible today.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core parity for historical runner occupancy[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bol